    "explanation": "PMS argv places per-input options BEFORE each -i. For the SRT input (input 1) it sets `-ss 1816 -analyzeduration 20000000 -probesize 20000000` so ffmpeg seeks the SRT alongside the source. The earlier rewriter dropped only `-i temp-0.srt` (2 args) and left the preceding `-ss 1816 -analyzeduration -probesize` block in place. Per ffmpeg argv spec those options apply to the NEXT -i, but with no next -i they re-bind as positional output options on the LAST -i. -ss <T> as output seek means: discard output frames before time T. With -copyts stripped on HLS, output PTS starts at 0 and never reaches 1816 → every encoded frame discarded → segment muxer waits indefinitely → Plex Android sees no segments → 'Connection error'.",
